    docs(02-click-retention): ADR-0011 and ADR-0018 no longer claim neither job interrupts JDBC
    
    The 02-click-retention amendment to ADR-0011 and ADR-0018's shutdown consequence said neither
    background job interrupts a JDBC call. That is false for the click writer: ClickRecorder.close
    calls shutdownNow after its 5 s drain, which interrupts a running insert, and ADR-0011's own
    shutdown section already says so (a running insert may ignore the interrupt and commit, hence
    'outcome unknown'). Only the purge never interrupts: it waits up to 3 s for a run in progress.
    Both ADRs now state each job's behaviour. Wording only; no design or behaviour change.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

